{"word": "lounge", "source": "freedictionaryapi", "data": {"word": "lounge", "entries": [{"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "verb", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈlaʊ̯nd͡ʒ/", "tags": ["General American", "Received Pronunciation"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈlæʊ̯nd͡ʒ/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ˈlaːnd͡ʒ/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/lɔɲdʒ/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/lawɲdʒ/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/laʊnd͡ʒ/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/lɔnd͡ʒ/", "tags": ["proscribed"]}], "forms": [{"word": "lounges", "tags": ["present", "singular", "third-person"]}, {"word": "lounging", "tags": ["participle", "present"]}, {"word": "lounged", "tags": ["participle", "past"]}, {"word": "lounged", "tags": ["past"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "(intransitive) To relax; to spend time lazily; to stand, sit, or recline, in an indolent manner.", "tags": ["intransitive"], "examples": ["We like to spend our Sundays lounging about at home in our pyjamas."], "quotes": [{"text": "We lounge over the sciences, dawdle through literature, yawn over politics.", "reference": "1854, J. Hannay, Singleton Fontenoy, R.N:"}, {"text": "Everybody knows they have times when they wanna just lay back / Kick their feet up, y'know / Listen to some good music and just lounge / That's right, I said lounge", "reference": "1993, “Loungin'”, in Guru's Jazzmatazz, Vol. 1, performed by Guru ft. Donald Byrd:"}, {"text": "On Professor Solanka’s street, well-heeled white youths lounged in baggy garments on roseate stoops, stylishly simulating indigence while they waited for the billionairedom that would surely be along sometime soon.", "reference": "2001, Salman Rushdie, Fury: A Novel, London: Jonathan Cape, →ISBN, page 4:"}], "synonyms": ["loll"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "безделнича"}, {"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "раз